---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import StudentLoanCalculator from '@/components/tools/calc/StudentLoanCalculator.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="student-loan-calculator">
  <StudentLoanCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the student loan calculator works</h2>
    <p>
      The student loan calculator uses the standard repayment formula <code>M = P × i ÷ (1 − (1 + i)^−n)</code>,
      where <code>P</code> is the balance, <code>i</code> is the yearly rate divided by 12 and <code>n</code> is the
      number of months. Each month the interest is the balance times <code>i</code>, and the rest of the payment and
      any extra payment reduce the balance.
    </p>
    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      A 35,000 balance at 6.5% over 10 years has a payment of 397.42 a month. You repay 47,690.02 in total, of which
      12,690.02 is interest. Paying 100 more each month ends the loan after 89 payments and saves 3,503.91 of interest.
    </p>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      The calculator shows a standard fixed-rate plan. Income-driven, graduated and extended plans, forgiveness
      programs and the tax deduction for student loan interest are not included. If interest built up while you were
      in school, enter the balance after it was added.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
